NAME
	scene-view (display) - draw a 2-D scene (entities, features, layers, trails, clock) in a geo or xy frame, with a camera shared through scenefs

INTERFACE
	display (MatrixDisplay, MatrixTicker 100 ms)

READS
	meta		ndb stanza: frame=(geo|xy) projection= units=
			title= trail= bounds=
	time		the scene clock (one number)
	entities/<id>	ndb stanza: x= y= (xy) or lat= lon= (geo),
			label= shape= color= group= course= size=
			stale= trail= dim= (kind= affil= also understood)
	features/<id>	ndb stanza: type=(point|polyline|polygon|circle)
			points= radius= color= fill= width= dash= label=
	layers/<id>	ndb stanza: kind=grid step= color=,
			kind=image file= bounds= opacity=, or
			kind=scene dir= opacity= (another scene, stacked)
			hide=1 on any object hides it
	status, view	when the mount is a scenefs (docs/scene-design.md §3)

WRITES
	<mount>/ctl	when the mount is a scenefs: center, zoom, select,
			deselect, unfollow on this pane's pan, zoom and
			click; play, pause, step, seek, live on its keys

DESCRIPTION
	Renders through lib/scene: anti-aliased shapes, heading arrows,
	fading trails, labels placed without overlap, a scale bar, and
	a HUD with the frame, zoom, clock and playback mode.  Entities
	past their stale= time are drawn dimmed.

	On a scenefs mount the pane reloads only when status reports a
	new gen, adopts the server's camera (so agents writing ctl move
	the picture), and publishes its own; a fit request (ctl fit) is
	answered by each viewer for its own size.  On a plain directory
	it rescans on a count+mtime change and the camera is local.

	Keys: + - zoom, h j k l pan, f fit, space play/pause, . step,
	, step back, L live.  Pointer: drag pans, wheel zooms about the
	pointer, click selects.

SEE ALSO
	scene-fixture, geo-fixture, scenefs(4), scenerender(1), scene(2)
